    "q-314205": {
      "dom_id": "step-q314205",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)={(6x-5)}^{6},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let $g(x)=6x-5$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{6}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{6})^{′}=6{g}^{5}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(6x-5)^{′}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =6{g}^{5}\\cdot (6) \\\\  & =36(6x-5)^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
